adb: start USB transports on the device, detached start is host-only

AOSP 36c8520873d5 ("Add attach/detach support to libusb backend") makes
fdevent_register_transport() put every kTransportUsb transport into
kCsDetached. The check is only guarded by ADB_HOST for the
usb_devices_start_detached() part, so on the device (ADB_HOST=0) the
legacy FunctionFS transport (transport_legacy.cpp sets kTransportUsb) is
never started: no read/write threads, host shows the device as "offline".
Upstream adbd is unaffected only because its aio transport keeps
type == kTransportAny.

Seen on GT-N8010 (kernel 3.4, legacy FFS) with Build 33: adbd logs
"registering usb transport" and nothing else, `adb devices` says offline.

--- a/transport.cpp
+++ b/transport.cpp
@@ -751,19 +751,20 @@
     if (t->GetConnectionState() != kCsNoPerm) {
         t->connection()->SetTransport(t);
 
-        if (t->type == kTransportUsb
 #if ADB_HOST
-            && usb_devices_start_detached()  // -d setting propagated from the
-                                             // host device, hence n/a on-device.
-#endif
-        ) {
+        // Detached start is a host-side feature (-d / ADB_LIBUSB_START_DETACHED).
+        // On the device every registered transport must be started, otherwise
+        // the legacy FunctionFS transport (type == kTransportUsb) never gets
+        // its read/write threads and the host sees the device as "offline".
+        if (t->type == kTransportUsb && usb_devices_start_detached()) {
             t->SetConnectionState(kCsDetached);
         } else {
             t->connection()->Start();
-#if ADB_HOST
             send_connect(t);
-#endif
         }
+#else
+        t->connection()->Start();
+#endif
     }
 
     {
